# fixedbugs, defect 2351, lane b25-pkgc, 2026-11-08.
#
# A fetched package's header naming one the package does not ship, which the
# program has at its root. A fetched package's unit searches the runtime, its
# own `package` groups' answer and its own root, never the program's folders
# (panel 235's R9, its C1), so the program's file does not stand in for it:
# the header clang did not find there is named, and where it was looked for,
# before anything of the package compiles (C2), clang's own words unprinted.
use <pk>/pk

function main()
    print(pk.v())
